{title: Jesus Christ Is Risen Today}
{artist: Lyra Davidica (1708), Charles Wesley}
{genre: Easter}
{style: Anthem}
{flow: Opening}
{key: C}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{score: jesus-christ-is-risen-today.abc}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Open Hymnal score (Jesus_Christ_Is_Risen_Today-Easter_Hymn)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Jesus [G]Christ [C]is [F]risen to[C]day, Al__[Dm]__le[G]lu[C]ia!
[F]Our [C]tri[F]umphant [Dm]ho[C]ly [G]day, [C]Al__[Dm]__le[G]lu[C]ia!
[G]Who did once, up[C]on the cross, [G]Al__[D7]__lelu[G]ia!
[G]Suffer [C]to re[F]deem our [C]loss, Al[Em]le[G]lu[C]ia!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Hymns of [G]praise [C]then [F]let us [C]sing, Al__[Dm]__le[G]lu[C]ia!
[F]Un[C]to [F]Christ, our [Dm]hea[C]venly [G]king, [C]Al__[Dm]__le[G]lu[C]ia!
[G]Who endured the [C]cross and grave, [G]Al__[D7]__lelu[G]ia!
[G]Sinners [C]to re[F]deem and [C]save, Al[Em]le[G]lu[C]ia!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]But the [G]pains [C]which [F]He en[C]dured, Al__[Dm]__le[G]lu[C]ia!
[F]Our [C]sal[F]vation [Dm]hath [C]pro[G]cured, [C]Al__[Dm]__le[G]lu[C]ia!
[G]Now above the [C]sky He’s king, [G]Al__[D7]__lelu[G]ia!
[G]Where the [C]angels [F]ever [C]sing, Al[Em]le[G]lu[C]ia!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]Sing we [G]to [C]our [F]God a[C]bove, Al__[Dm]__le[G]lu[C]ia!
[F]Praise [C]e[F]ternal [Dm]as [C]His [G]love, [C]Al__[Dm]__le[G]lu[C]ia!
[G]Praise Him, all you [C]heavenly host, [G]Al__[D7]__lelu[G]ia!
[G]Father, [C]Son, and [F]Holy [C]Ghost, Al[Em]le[G]lu[C]ia!
{end_of_verse}
